{"skill":{"slug":"openclaw-nextcloud","displayName":"openclaw-nextcloud"},"version":{"version":"0.8.0","createdAt":1791791309190,"changelog":"- Version updated to 0.8.0.\n- Better handling of binary uploads and downloads.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":24567,"sha256":"4bce6632cb8e73d1b94154c6b1f44f77229cdfc4a4bf49cedce19339b533b582","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":23530,"sha256":"eadf087258ae3fbfb1b880d0823d0d39957925ad85de470dd8f83cef8ec1ee45","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"index.js","size":139902,"sha256":"e738d9a73f1f910fe0d531f1524c85d4fb2c8aa7a47b3f1a02016a52ca4d2fed","contentType":"application/x-javascript"},{"path":"package.json","size":631,"sha256":"3a6fb943b0feb54eb1a25c10bf5f70dc0353971ea6e7961cd089300683d40adf","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"package-lock.json","size":19608,"sha256":"83f369a2f4b626435f8d2a492be46c305892ac97373aca66e77fadb6c4c55deb","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/nextcloud.js","size":794236,"sha256":"05c1c7d18d96e0da70c7816ff409caf66a7c6ca67df92edcd4be58799a6552b0","contentType":"application/x-javascript"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2011,"sha256":"67a8de0b12781ea1750cadb304e78ee9ac942337829b28031c2411bdd2d6217e","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1791792017862,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"8eb5528e0519abf8e460058283190f026c67914a0a75a026871e47a4033c2d58","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/8eb5528e0519abf8e460058283190f026c67914a0a75a026871e47a4033c2d58","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1791791808958},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":17,"checkedAt":1791792017862},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a broad Nextcloud account-management skill, but its credential use, destructive actions, and public-link sharing are disclosed and bounded by user-facing safety guidance and CLI confirmation tokens.","dimensions":[{"detail":"NEXTCLOUD_URL, NEXTCLOUD_USER, NEXTCLOUD_TOKEN, and optional NEXTCLOUD_EMAIL are purpose-aligned. Source and bundle send authenticated requests to URLs derived from NEXTCLOUD_URL, enforce HTTPS except localhost or explicit OPENCLAW_ALLOW_HTTP=1, and show no telemetry or unrelated host calls.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No runtime install hook or remote code fetch is required for normal use; package.json has no postinstall/preinstall script, and the packaged script is a bundled Node executable with pinned dependencies recorded in package-lock.json.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill instructs agents to confirm destructive and public-facing operations, treat retrieved Nextcloud content as untrusted data, and use stored defaults only after the user opts in. Some recoverable writes rely on agent/user confirmation rather than a CLI token, but this is disclosed.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill uses an account-level Nextcloud app password and can read, modify, delete, upload, and publicly share user content. This is high impact but disclosed, purpose-aligned, revocable through a Nextcloud app password, and protected for irreversible/public-share commands by --confirm tokens.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The package purpose is coherent: a Node.js CLI manages Nextcloud notes, tasks, calendars, files, contacts, shares, and Deck boards via documented Nextcloud APIs. Public sharing and account-level app-password scope are explicitly disclosed in SKILL.md and README.md.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving the skill an account-level Nextcloud app password. Use a dedicated app password, prefer a test account first, keep NEXTCLOUD_URL on HTTPS, and be especially careful with delete commands and shares create-link because public links can expose files outside your account.","findings":"[TP4] expected: The date-fns/XML/parser code is bundled dependency code inside scripts/nextcloud.js, not a separate hidden capability. The inspected source and manifest implement the declared Nextcloud CLI behavior.\n[AE1] expected: The referenced scripts/nextcloud.js file is present and was inspected at relevant source and bundled enforcement points; the prior partial-inspection signal is not evidence of evasion in this workspace.\n[LP1] expected: Environment-variable reads and network egress are necessary for an authenticated Nextcloud client and are explicitly declared in compatibility and OpenClaw metadata, including credential scope and egress target.\n[SDI-2] expected: Public link creation, including optional edit permission, is a real high-impact capability, but SKILL.md and README.md disclose it, warn that links expose data, default permissions to read, and require --confirm shares:create-link.\n[SDI-1] expected: The current artifact metadata and documentation do mention shares/public links, including list/create/delete commands, permissions, password-file, expiry, and confirmation requirements, so this is not hidden in the inspected artifact.\n[EA2] expected: The 'without asking' text applies only after the user chooses to save default calendars/address books/boards; it is scoped preference memory, not autonomous destructive action.\n[SQP-2] expected: Delete operations are real, but main() calls requireExplicitConfirmation before dispatch and the destructive command set requires exact --confirm action tokens. Documentation also tells agents to confirm exact targets with the user.\n[YR4] expected: The matched text appears in bundled dependency pattern descriptions, not exploit execution or offensive tooling. I found no eval, child_process execution, persistence hook, or unrelated outbound endpoint in the inspected source.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1791792017862}}}}}